            {
              "id": "627e7c00-990b-4430-90bc-d742c336a586",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": "<em><strong>Exodus to the Virtual World: How Online Fun Is Changing Reality</strong></em> was written by Edward Castronova, published by St. Martin's Griffin, November 11, 2008."
            },
            {
              "id": "3ea85935-3fd7-4145-9984-c1b800a936d0",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "88693a18-c1eb-48d4-b345-13c9467f7d6f",
              "type": "quote",
              "html": "<em>Virtual worlds have exploded out of online game culture and now capture the attention of millions of ordinary people: husbands, wives, fathers, mothers, workers, retirees. Devoting dozens of hours each week to massively multiplayer virtual reality environments (like </em>World of Warcraft<em> and </em>Second Life<em>), these millions are the start of an exodus into the refuge of fantasy, where they experience life under a new social, political, and economic order built around fun. Given the choice between a fantasy world and the real world, how many of us would choose reality? </em>Exodus to the Virtual World<em><br> explains the growing migration into virtual reality, and how it will change the way we live--both in fantasy worlds and in the real one.</em>"
            }
          ]
        },
